  "details": "As a world/Udon creator, I need to test synchronized multiplayer features requiring 4 concurrent players on a single machine. The VRChat SDK explicitly documents supporting up to 8 local test clients. However, when the 4th client attempts to join the test instance, it is rejected by the server with:\n\nOnJoinRoomFailed(32752, \"You cannot enter this instance at this time, please try again later\")\n\nThe client then falls back to TryAlternateInstance and creates a separate private room, isolating the 4th client. It appears that the Photon backend enforces a 3-connection per-IP cap per instance, which conflicts with local multi-client developer testing.\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\nLaunch 3 VRChat desktop clients on one machine and have them join the same private/test instance. (Succeeds)\n\nLaunch a 4th desktop client on the same machine and accept the invite to that same instance.\n\nNotice the 4th client fails to enter and gets redirected to an alternate private instance.",
